---

### 1. ABA Problem Scenario

The ABA problem occurs when a pointer that was previously loaded is stored back into a location, but the value at that location has changed in between. In this case, the `top` pointer can be modified by another thread between the time it's loaded and when it's stored back, causing the compare-and-swap to succeed even though the stack structure has changed.

Consider this sequence:
1. Thread A loads `top` (say it points to node X)
2. Thread B pops node X, pushes node Y, then pops Y and pushes X back
3. Thread A now tries to pop X using `compare_exchange_weak` with `top.load()` as expected value
4. The operation succeeds even though the stack structure has changed

### 2. Incorrect Behavior

The incorrect behavior is that Thread A will pop a node that has already been popped and potentially freed by another thread. This leads to use-after-free errors or undefined behavior.

### 3. Fix using Tagged Pointers

```c
struct Node { int val; Node* next; };
struct TaggedPtr {
    Node* ptr;
    int tag;
};
atomic<TaggedPtr> top;

void push(int v) {
    TaggedPtr expected, desired;
    do {
        expected = top.load();
        desired.ptr = new Node{v, expected.ptr};
        desired.tag = expected.tag + 1;
    } while (!top.compare_exchange_weak(expected, desired));
}

int pop() {
    TaggedPtr expected, desired;
    do {
        expected = top.load();
        if (!expected.ptr) return -1;
        desired.ptr = expected.ptr->next;
        desired.tag = expected.tag + 1;
    } while (!top.compare_exchange_weak(expected, desired));
    int val = expected.ptr->val;
    delete expected.ptr;
    return val;
}
```

### 4. Alternative Fix using Hazard Pointers

```c
// Simplified version using hazard pointers
struct Node { int val; Node* next; };
atomic<Node*> top;

// Hazard pointer array (simplified)
atomic<Node*>* hazard_ptrs = new atomic<Node*>[MAX_THREADS];

void push(int v) {
    Node* n = new Node{v, top.load()};
    while (!top.compare_exchange_weak(n->next, n));
}

int pop() {
    Node* t = top.load();
    while (t && !top.compare_exchange_weak(t, t->next)) {
        // Hazard pointer protection
        hazard_ptrs[get_thread_id()].store(t);
        // Re-check after hazard pointer set
        t = top.load();
    }
    if (t) {
        // Clear hazard pointer
        hazard_ptrs[get_thread_id()].store(nullptr);
        int val = t->val;
        delete t;
        return val;
    }
    return -1;
}
```

